  "Id": 1790,
  "Title": "Sarah Bowen Savant Promoted to Full Professor",
  "NewsSubTitle": null,
  "NewsSummary": "Sarah Bowen Savant has been promoted to full professor at AKU-ISMC",
  "GlobalNews": false,
  "AlternateNewsTitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSubtitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSummary": null,
  "NewsContent": "<div class=\"ExternalClassFA94C7EBD243468AAF2B7559834D7484\"><p>We are very pleased to announce that Sarah Bowen Savant has been promoted to full professor!</p><div>Sarah Bowen Savant is a cultural historian specialising in early Islam, the study of religion, historiography, late antique Iran and Iraq and prophetic biography. She is also the Principle Investigator of <a href=\"http&#58;//kitab-project.org/?fbclid=IwAR3gcVlLODx-_SPvi1PcYk2TRbLxCI42J1FAXx6XR8-5t-Y04ZrnBpPUZJE\" target=\"_blank\">KITAB</a> Project.</div><div><br></div><div>Professor Savant&#160; received her MA from the University of Chicago and her PhD from Harvard University. Prior to joining AKU-ISMC in 2007, she was a Sultan Post-Doctoral Fellow at the University of California, Berkeley. She is the author of <em>The New Muslims of Post-Conquest Iran&#58; Tradition, Memory, and Conversion </em>(Cambridge&#58; Cambridge University Press, 2013), which won the Saidi-Sirjani Book Award, given by the International Society for Iranian Studies on behalf of the Persian Heritage Foundation.&#160;</div><div><br></div><div>For further information about Professor Savant, please click <a href=\"/ismc/faculty/pages/profile.aspx?ProfileID=1&amp;Name=Sarah%20Bowen%20Savant\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.<br></div></div>",
